@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+# Orange Pi 4 Pro EDK2 v4 framebuffer coherence fix
+
+## Physical symptom
+
+V3 reached `UEFI Interactive Shell v2.2` and the `Shell>` prompt, but HDMI
+showed fragmented glyphs and stale horizontal pieces while UART text was
+correct.
+
+## Root cause
+
+The active vendor framebuffer at `0xBBF11000` is inside LPDDR5. The initial
+A733 virtual-memory table mapped all LPDDR5 as write-back cacheable RAM. The
+sunxi display engine scans that memory without hardware CPU-cache coherence,
+while the stock EDK2 `LcdGraphicsOutputDxe` writes pixels with normal memory
+stores and does not clean the AArch64 data cache after every GOP BLT.
+
+## Fix
+
+V4 installs a later, page-aligned MMU descriptor for exactly
+`0xBBF11000..0xBC169000` (`0x258000` bytes) using
+`ARM_MEMORY_REGION_ATTRIBUTE_UNCACHED_UNBUFFERED`. The remaining 4 GiB RAM
+stays write-back cacheable. This trades framebuffer write speed for reliable
+scan-out and avoids modifying the generic EDK2 GOP driver.
+
+V4 keeps the compact Shell command set so the firmware still fits the fixed
+4 MiB image. The optional `map` command therefore remains absent. V4 does
+replace invalid boot discovery policy `0x3F` with the standard
+`BDP_CONNECT_ALL` value `2`.
+
+## Still open
+
+The A733 EHCI host controller still fails the generic EDK2 reset/start path.
+That is independent from HDMI coherence and remains a later hardware-driver
+milestone.
diff -ruN /tmp/opi-v3-reference/Platform/OrangePi/OrangePi4ProPkg/Library/A733VirtMemInfoLib/A733VirtMemInfoLib.c /mnt/data/opi4pro-uefi-v4/work/Platform/OrangePi/OrangePi4ProPkg/Library/A733VirtMemInfoLib/A733VirtMemInfoLib.c
--- /tmp/opi-v3-reference/Platform/OrangePi/OrangePi4ProPkg/Library/A733VirtMemInfoLib/A733VirtMemInfoLib.c	2026-07-29 01:01:45.000000000 +0000
+++ /mnt/data/opi4pro-uefi-v4/work/Platform/OrangePi/OrangePi4ProPkg/Library/A733VirtMemInfoLib/A733VirtMemInfoLib.c	2026-07-29 10:14:32.621896435 +0000
@@ -49,5 +49,23 @@
   Table[3].Length       = FixedPcdGet32 (PcdFvSize) + 0x8000;
   Table[3].Attributes   = ARM_MEMORY_REGION_ATTRIBUTE_WRITE_BACK_RO;
 
+  // The HDMI display engine is not cache-coherent with the CPU.  The broad
+  // LPDDR5 descriptor above maps this range as write-back RAM, which leaves
+  // freshly rendered glyphs in CPU cache lines and produces torn/fragmented
+  // text on HDMI.  This later descriptor deliberately overrides the active
+  // scan-out buffer with an uncached mapping.  It is slower than write-back,
+  // but deterministic and correct for the first hardware port.
+  Table[4].PhysicalBase = FixedPcdGet64 (PcdFrameBufferBase);
+  Table[4].VirtualBase  = Table[4].PhysicalBase;
+  Table[4].Length       = FixedPcdGet32 (PcdFrameBufferSize);
+  Table[4].Attributes   = ARM_MEMORY_REGION_ATTRIBUTE_UNCACHED_UNBUFFERED;
+
+  DEBUG ((
+    DEBUG_INFO,
+    "A733 MMU: framebuffer %lx..%lx mapped UNCACHED\n",
+    Table[4].PhysicalBase,
+    Table[4].PhysicalBase + Table[4].Length
+    ));
+
   *VirtualMemoryMap = Table;
 }
